  "goodToKnow": "Die Weltausstellung is a world's fair or Expo. Germany has hosted only one, the Expo 2000 in Hanover, which drew fewer visitors than hoped. Famous earlier fairs left landmarks, such as the Eiffel Tower (Paris, 1889) and the Atomium (Brussels, 1958). Germany is better known for its Messen (trade fairs), with Hanover, Frankfurt and Cologne among the largest venues. Plural: die Weltausstellungen."
